ing sure that it's  um uh delivered and administered before  its expiration date that there are  enough people to administer those  vaccines at the site  so yeah this is um the  um  our vaccine allocation  tool there was a lot of hesitancy from  the ministry initially about using R and  are shiny as a lot of you might know  that normally in public health care  especially in Africa countries tend to  use dhis2 platform so they were  extremely hesitant to you know work with  a new platform a separate one for their  covid-19 vaccination means but once they  saw what we did to bring them on board  was that before we even got any data  from the country we built a mock app we  travel to the country we had a training  uh requirements Gathering Workshop we  showed them the app they were able to  use it and see how useful it can be for  their decision making and that was  essentially all we needed to get them on  board and since then they have been  um extremely active and instrumental in  ensuring that we receive all the data  that we need we have regular meetings  with the Ministry of Health folks and  their covid-19 task force to ensure that  they are abreast with all the changes  that are happening that we are making to  the model  and um we are still figuring out some of  the challenges with uh transitioning  this tool over to the country team like  I said you know they  this is a new tool for them they don't  have our programmers on their team so we  will we're continuing to work with the  ministry  to figure out those challenges  but yeah and  that's where my talk ends I is I would  like to advertise  um this a little bit since I got a  chance that I am hiring a senior  associate in data science ours is a  small but growing theme and we work on  very interesting problems we don't have  huge data sets but we do have uh we do  build very interesting uh models so do  get in touch with me if you have any if  you're interested  great it's like anybody  [Music]

